  "id": "ua-pulaski-technical-college-aas-surgical-technology",
  "major": "Surgical Technology",
  "notes": "Program located at the Main UA-Pulaski Tech Campus in North Little Rock. Accredited by the Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs (CAAHEP). Graduates are eligible to sit for the Certified Surgical Technologist Exam (completion does not ensure certification). Admission is competitive: students are selected after December final grades based on cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher from all high school/college transcripts plus an interview; 18 full-time students accepted each academic year. A drug screen and background check are required of all selected students. A grade of C or better is required to continue in the professional program; minimum 2.0 GPA required for graduation. Additional prerequisite courses may be required if minimum placement test scores are not met. This standalone AAS is distinct from the BHCLR Surgical Technology completion option (taught through Baptist Health College Little Rock).",
